WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.286
Exposure management starts with an inventory of important accounts, profiles, domains, repositories, public documents, services, and third-party references.

00:00:09.286 --> 00:00:20.000
Review them as an external visitor would, then compare what is visible with what the person or organization intends to disclose.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:32.142
Individuals can tighten privacy settings, remove unnecessary contact or location details, close unused accounts, review old posts, and keep professional profiles accurate and consistent.

00:00:32.142 --> 00:00:40.952
Strong unique passwords and multi-factor authentication reduce the chance that an existing footprint becomes an account compromise.

00:00:40.952 --> 00:00:44.523
Review photographs and documents before publication.

00:00:44.523 --> 00:00:52.856
Remove unnecessary metadata where appropriate, check visible backgrounds and embedded comments, and use approved organizational templates.

00:00:52.856 --> 00:00:58.332
Avoid sharing schedules, credentials, private addresses, or security-sensitive operational details.

00:00:58.332 --> 00:01:03.808
Organizations need recurring review processes rather than one cleanup event.

00:01:03.808 --> 00:01:09.761
Assign owners for public assets, domains, repositories, documents, and social accounts.

00:01:09.761 --> 00:01:17.618
Integrate exposure checks into publishing, employee onboarding and departure, project closure, procurement, and incident response.

00:01:17.618 --> 00:01:26.427
Employee awareness should explain why ordinary public details can combine into risk without encouraging fear or secrecy.

00:01:26.427 --> 00:01:31.903
Provide clear reporting channels for suspected exposure and respond constructively.

00:01:31.903 --> 00:01:39.284
Monitoring should focus on organizational assets and authorized purposes, not covert surveillance of staff.

00:01:39.284 --> 00:01:42.379
Track remediation and verify results.

00:01:42.379 --> 00:01:50.712
Some third-party copies or indexes may persist, so record residual risk and follow appropriate removal processes.

00:01:50.712 --> 00:02:00.474
The goal is a deliberate footprint that supports legitimate communication and operations while reducing avoidable privacy and security exposure.
